"""
BixBench bix-24-q2 -- CBD metabolic effects in CRC cells.
Question: Using DE (padj<0.05, |log2FC|>0.5) and GO Biological Process
enrichment, determine whether UP- or DOWN-regulation of genes primarily drives
the metabolic effects of CBD treatment in CRC cells.

Primary comparison : CBD_IC50 (group 7, n=3) vs DMSO (group 3, n=3, vehicle).
Sensitivities      : CBD_IC50 vs Untreated (group 1); CBD_IC50_Serum_starvation
                     (group 8) vs DMSO_Serum_starvation (group 4).

Environment constraints (facts): no R/DESeq2/edgeR/clusterProfiler; no network;
no GO annotation databases; only pandas/numpy/scipy/statsmodels. The DE analysis
is therefore a native Python DESeq2-paradigm implementation (median-of-ratios
size factors, per-gene NB dispersion with shrinkage to a dispersion-mean trend,
Wald test with NB variance, BH-adjusted padj). GO-BP enrichment uses an OFFLINE,
hand-curated human metabolic GO-BP annotation (GO:0008152 subtree; the MAIN
limitation of this study) mapped to Ensembl IDs, tested by hypergeometric/Fisher
tests with BH-adjusted p-values.

ASSUMPTIONS (per approved plan):
 * CBD-treated = 'CBD_IC50' (group 7); vehicle control = 'DMSO' (group 3).
 * 3 samples/group are unpaired biological replicates -> unpaired two-group NB.
 * Rows are Ensembl ENSG IDs, mapped directly into the GO table (no conversion).
 * Normalization = median-of-ratios on subset; pre-filter total >= 10 in subset;
   DE threshold padj<0.05 AND |log2FC|>0.5 (up>0.5, down<-0.5); padj = BH FDR.
 * GO enrichment universe = post-filter expressed genes.
"""
import math, json
